  "terminology":[
    "Acute gastric dilatation and gastric dilatation-volvulus are distinct authored states.",
    "GDV is a rapidly progressive life-threatening emergency requiring simultaneous stabilization and surgical routing.",
    "Breed, deep chest, meal or family history change risk but never establish diagnosis.",
    "Nonproductive retching, progressive distension, poor pulses, collapse or shock trigger emergency action before a long history.",
    "Radiography is obtained only when transport and positioning are safe; equivocal or unsafe imaging cannot silently close GDV suspicion.",
    "Laboratory and lactate trends support monitoring/prognosis and do not delay decompression or surgery.",
    "Decompression is pressure relief and stabilization, not definitive treatment of confirmed volvulus.",
    "Gastric and splenic viability, resection uncertainty and postoperative organ risk remain specialist-authored.",
    "Gastropexy reduces future volvulus risk but does not prevent all future gastric dilatation.",
    "Delay consequences remain linked to the original episode, not a random new patient.",
    "No fluid dose, decompression technique, anesthesia plan, gastropexy technique or tissue-resection threshold is generated."
  ],
